<title>UK: Allied Domecq to cut 700 jobs - paper.</title>
<headline>Allied Domecq to cut 700 jobs - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allied Domecq, the UK food and drinks group, is to shed 700 jobs in a worldwide restructuring operation aimed at saving around 15 million stg a year, a British newspaper said on Sunday.</p>
<p>In a three year project headed by Allied's director of taxation Peter Lyster, the firm will seek to shorten communication lines and improve information flows to the management, the Independent on Sunday said.</p>
<p>It said the firm was aiming to have just one finance department reposible for each continent by the end of the project.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 2774</p>
